## Part A — Punch list (feed this to your agent as-is)

### 1. Missing persistent "paper trading" banner on the Live Execution monitor — do this first

**Files:** `app/app/live/page.tsx`, `components/bot/live-tab.tsx`

Your own spec (`03 - Page by page features` §12, and the Risk Disclosure requirement in §23) is explicit: the live monitor needs *"Clear, persistent banner: 'Paper trading — no real funds are being used' (unless/until the account has an explicitly verified real-fund tier active, in which case the banner instead clearly states real capital is at risk)."*

Today, `app/app/bots/[botId]/backtest/[runId]/page.tsx` correctly shows an inline disclaimer ("Backtest results describe the past. They do not forecast or guarantee future performance."), but the live monitor has no equivalent. It has an "Emergency Stop" kill switch (good, satisfies that requirement) and a small "Live Paper Execution Feed" label in the empty state of `live-tab.tsx`, but no persistent banner stating no real funds are at risk.

Add a persistent, non-dismissable banner at the top of `app/app/live/page.tsx` (above or alongside the "Top Header Bar") and the equivalent spot in `components/bot/live-tab.tsx`'s active (non-empty) state. Since there is no real-fund tier implemented anywhere in this codebase yet, the banner is unconditional for now: something like an amber/informational strip reading "Paper trading only — no real funds are being used." Match the visual pattern of an existing inline alert/banner elsewhere in the app rather than hand-rolling new markup (check if `components/ui/misc.tsx` or the legal-page layout already has an `Alert`/banner primitive you can reuse).

### 2. Component-count copy overstates what's actually built

**File:** `components/builder/library-panel.tsx` (search placeholder, currently `"Search 100+ nodes"`)

`mock/layers.ts` currently defines exactly **68** components across **12** layers. `components/landing/hero.tsx` already gets this right — it says "12 layers · 60+ components," which is accurate. The library panel's placeholder is the one place still saying "100+," which was flagged as "ahead of schedule" as far back as `00 - START HERE` and never corrected. Change it to match the honest copy already used on the landing page (`"Search 60+ components"` or a neutral `"Search components"` that won't need editing every time you add one).

### 3. Stale leftover comment

