A `{/* TODO(phase5): detail page at /app/marketplace/:id */}` comment sits directly above a link that already correctly points at `/app/marketplace/${preset.id}` — the page it complains about not existing has existed since Phase 5. Delete the comment. Purely cosmetic, but it will confuse you or an agent later into thinking there's a real gap here.

### 4. Onboarding "Beginner" promise vs. actual behavior

**Files:** `app/onboarding/welcome/page.tsx`, `components/builder/inspector.tsx`

The welcome screen tells a Beginner-tier user: *"We will simplify complex nodes and keep advanced mathematical configs tucked away until you need them."* The selection is correctly saved (`setOnboardingAnswer({ experience: lvl })` → `useSession`'s `onboarding.experience`), but the only place that value is read anywhere in the app is `components/builder/inspector.tsx`, where it changes the "Deep Customization" button's visual variant (outline vs. secondary) — it does not actually hide or simplify anything. This isn't a broken button, it's copy making a promise the product doesn't keep.

Pick one:
- **(a) Cheap fix:** soften the onboarding copy to not promise hiding — e.g. "We'll highlight the settings that matter most for your level" — and leave the subtle variant change as the only effect.
- **(b) Real fix:** in `inspector.tsx`, when `onboarding.experience === 'beginner'`, actually collapse or visually de-emphasize non-essential `FieldDef`s in the "Core Parameters" list (you already have a `Deep Customization` modal that holds the advanced fields separately per Phase 6 — this may already be most of the way there structurally; check `field-renderer.tsx`/`deep-customization-dialog.tsx` for whether fields are already tagged with something like a `tier`/`advanced` flag you could gate on).

(a) is a five-minute fix; (b) is a real feature and can wait — but do one of them, don't leave the promise and the behavior mismatched.

